getting started with Google cloud  platform cloud sequel cloud sequel is a  fully managed database service that  makes it easy to set up  maintain manage and administer your  relational database in the cloud cloud  sequel offers high performance  scalability and convenience providing a  database infrastructure for applications  running anywhere to get started with  cloud sequel first go to the cloud  sequel instances page in the Google  cloud platform console and select your  project next click create instance click  my SQL and choose second generation  enter my instance for the instance ID  and a password for the root user you can  use default values for the other fields  and click create you'll return to the  instances list your new instance is  grayed out while it initializes and  starts up we can now connect to your  instance using the MySQL clients in the  cloud shell in the Google cloud platform  console click the cloud shell icon in  the upper right corner at the cloud  shell prompt connect to your cloud  sequel instance and enter your root  password you should now see the my  sequel prompt now that we're connected  we can perform operations on the  database create a sequel database on  your cloud sequel instance by typing  create database guestbook insert sample  data into the guestbook database and  retrieve the data by selecting select  star from entries congratulations you've  successfully created a cloud sequel  instance  [Music]
 

